{"id":"G2540","lemma":"καιρός","transliteration":"kairos","sayIt":"kairos","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, masculine","gloss":"time/right time","meaning":"καιρός, -οῦ, ὁ\n[in LXX chiefly for עֵת, also for מוֹעֵד, etc. ;]\n1. due measure, fitness, proportion (Eur., Xen., al.).\n2. Of Time (cl. also) in the sense of a fixed and definite period, time, season (Kennedy, Sources, 153): Mat.11:25, Mrk.1:15, Luk.21:8, Rom.13:11, Eph.6:18, Heb.11:15, 1Pe.1:5 1:11 Rev.1:3, al.; with genitive, πειρασμοῦ Luk.8:13; τ. καρπῶν, Mat.21:34; σύκων, Mrk.11:13; pl., Mat.21:41; χρόνοι ἢ (καὶ) κ., Act.1:7, 1Th.5:1; ἐθνῶν, Luk.21:24; of opportune or seasonable time, Act.24:25, Gal.6:10, Eph.5:16, Col.4:5; with inf., Heb.11:15; ὁ κ. οὗτος, Mrk.10:30, Luk.18:30; ὁ νῦν κ. (Dalman, Words, 148), Rom.8:18; ὁ κ. ὁ ἐμός, Jhn.7:6; κ. δεκτῲ, 2Co.6:2 (LXX); δουλεύειν τῷ κ., Rom.12:11, R, mg.; τ. σημεῖα τῶν κ., Mat.16:3; adverbial usages: ἐν κ., Mat.24:45, 1Pe.5:6 (cf. καιρῷ, Luk.20:10; τῷ κ., Mrk.12:2); ἄχρι καιροῦ, Luk.4:13; πρὸς καιρόν, Luk.8:13, 1Co.7:5; κατὰ καιρόν, Rom.5:6; πρὸ καιροῦ, Mat.8:29\nSYN.: (χρόνος) time in the sense of duration (AS)","glosses":["time","times","appointed time","harvest time","proper time","seasons"],"count":79,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":29,"renderings":{"bsb":"appointed time"}},{"chapterId":"mat-11","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"time","kjv":"time"}},{"chapterId":"mat-12","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"time","kjv":"time"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":30,"renderings":{"bsb":"At that time","kjv":"the time"}},{"chapterId":"mat-14","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"time","kjv":"time"}},{"chapterId":"mat-16","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"times"}},{"chapterId":"mat-21","v":34,"renderings":{"bsb":"harvest time","kjv":"the time"}},{"chapterId":"mat-21","v":41,"renderings":{"bsb":"harvest time"}},{"chapterId":"mat-24","v":45,"renderings":{"bsb":"the proper time"}},{"chapterId":"mat-26","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"time","kjv":"time"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-1","v":15,"renderings